# Project Model

- Privacy-first: no tracking, no ads. Sign-in is required to open, join or create anything: Google (openid only), Facebook (user ID only) or passkey. Never store email, real name or photo; provider IDs only as keyed hashes.
- Accounts have a private unique username and a profile name used on calendars by default, with a per-calendar override. Profile page (`account.html`): name, sign-in methods, calendars and Hubs, sign out, delete account.
- No PINs: the unique URL is the invite; the optional access emoji is an invite confirmation remembered per account. Old PIN names and Hubs are claimed once with their PIN, then the PIN is deleted.
- Anyone signed in with the link can open and join a calendar or Hub; the link is the only access control. The optional access emoji must be picked before a new account sees it, and is remembered per account afterwards.
- Organisers can Block (`users.blocked`) any person on a calendar: access paused, answers left out of views and Best Match, bookings still count.
- Respect the three privacy modes: Open (everyone sees all), Hidden (only organiser sees individual choices), Blind (nobody sees individual choices). Names are private on Blind, and on Hidden with "Hide names too": members see only themselves, the organisers and a total.
- Calendar model: 1-6 time slots, 1-5 status options (with weights and colours), date ranges up to 360 days.
- Auto-rank "Best Match" by weighted status scores, with expandable rosters.
- Calendar Hubs: one private link lists multiple calendars; opening a calendar from a Hub counts as Hub activity.
- Super admin panel manages calendars, Hubs, accounts, permanent retention, and site config (Setup tab).
- Go page opens a calendar or Hub by code or pasted URL.
